module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- evaluateWith : Strategy -> Expr -> a — the EXPLICIT-STRATEGY entry.
-- expr-substrate Phase 8 (brief:
-- `workstreams/expr-substrate/briefs/phase-8-explicit-strategy-evaluate.md`).
--
-- The VALUE-LEVEL sibling of the already-shipped block-scoped
-- `lazy {}` / `eager {}` / `partial {}` / `jit {}` form: `evaluateWith strategy
-- expr` evaluates `expr` under the named strategy, the explicit-argument way to
-- choose an evaluation strategy (the Lisp-`eval`-with-a-quoted-form analogue).
-- The block form selects a strategy by SCOPE (a `withInstance` frame walked by
-- `resolveEvaluator`); this entry selects by an EXPLICITLY-NAMED strategy — the
-- complement, sharing the same `Evaluator <strategy>.eval` method + the same 4
-- `*Eval` natives. No new evaluator, no new dispatch primitive, no new syntax —
-- plain function application over the existing registry.
--
-- THE DISPATCH IS `.fenel` (the no-new-TS-logic gate): the body resolves the
-- `Evaluator <strategy>` instance via `dispatchLookupOne` (the same dispatch
-- primitive the representation read-throughs in identifiable.fenel use), reads
-- its `.eval` method (the strategy function, by id string or by a `{$ref}`
-- reference — `evalApply`'s first parameter is typed as that function), and
-- hands off to the `evalApply` seam. Only the ctx-threaded
-- host-evaluator re-entry (`evalApply`, in the evaluator-strategies ffi leaf) is
-- native — see its decl for why a `.fenel` body cannot author it.
--
-- SIGNATURE NOTES (Step-0 audit, `notes/phase-8-audit.md`):
--   * `strategy` is the strategy entity's codeName STRING — the dispatch key
--     ("EagerStrategy" / "LazyStrategy" / "PartialStrategy" / "JitStrategy"),
--     matching `dispatchLookupOne`'s `target` + the instance `args[0]` markers.
--     There is NO closed `Strategy` ADT (RESOLVED, Rom 2026-06-11 — a strategy
--     IS an `Evaluator` instance keyed by its 1-case entity, dispatched by the
--     registry, NOT a sum a function pattern-matches). The 4 markers are not
--     registered as constructible catalog entities, so the string IS the
--     surface today. (A bare-value `evaluateWith EagerStrategy e` surface = a
--     recorded tail.)
--   * `expr` is typed `Expression` (live JSON-Logic AST) — what the 4 `*Eval`
--     natives consume. The language-honest `Expr`-typed signature + the
--     live-evaluator-over-`Expr` swap is a recorded tail (no `Expr -> Expression`
--     lowering ships; that's the escalation fence kept uncrossed).
--   * Returns `Result EvalError Value` (NOT bare `a`): the natives produce it,
--     it is no-throw / Fenel-first-honest, and an unknown/unwired strategy is a
--     clean `Err` (not a silent eager fallback). The `*Eval` Result flows
--     through unchanged on the hit path.
-- =========================================================================

@label "Evaluate with strategy"
@description "The explicit-strategy entry: evaluate a JSON-Logic Expression under a named evaluation strategy. `evaluateWith strategy expr` resolves the `Evaluator <strategy>` instance (strategy = the strategy entity's codeName string, e.g. \"PartialStrategy\"), reads its `eval` method, and applies it to `expr`, returning the strategy's `Result EvalError Value`. The value-level sibling of the block-scoped `lazy {}` / `partial {}` forms (which select a strategy by scope) — this one selects by explicit argument. An unknown strategy surfaces a clean `Err InternalError`, never a silent eager fallback. expr-substrate Phase 8; the dispatch is `.fenel`, only the ctx-threaded `evalApply` re-entry is native."
@tags "engine" "evaluator" "strategy" "evaluate" "expr-substrate" "phase-8"
evaluateWith : (strategy: String) -> (expr: Expression) -> Result EvalError Value
evaluateWith strategy expr = case dispatchLookupOne "Evaluator" strategy of
  Just methods -> evalApply methods.eval expr
  Nothing -> Err (InternalError { message = cat "evaluateWith: no Evaluator instance for strategy " strategy })
